From 910463c09f411daaa3a3809403cc5348a3828e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:57:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui_gateway): hand pending automation replays to the
 successor on retirement [daveey]

A failed automation turn's one delayed replay lived only in the process that
scheduled it. When that backend was retired (superseded always-on / boot commit
behind the checkout) every `_fire` was refused as "busy", spent the busy budget
and, after BUSY_RECHECKS_MAX, dropped the mixed process_complete + kanban_notice
delivery with no model replay (hub chat 20260101_000000_abc123, Jan 01 00:00-00:02 UTC).

Five whys: the chat stayed unresolved(turn_failed) -> the retry was dropped ->
retirement was counted as a busy chat -> custody was process-local with no
successor owner -> no test crossed predecessor -> successor.

Fix: a retired process hands each pending replay (stable item ids, original
payload/due/attempt/persisted) to the chat's exact profile state.db
(automation_replay_handoff.Journal) on retire_host_loops, on schedule while
retired, and on every retired timer fire; local custody is dropped only after
the journal accepted it, a storage failure keeps it and spends no budget.
The producer-admission pass of the live backend consumes due batches through
the ordinary wake admission (`_wake_session_turn(profiles=[exact profile])`),
claim-fenced; a refused admission leaves the batch pending. A successful turn
(context-start watermark) and an explicit user Stop fence handed-off custody;
shutdown does not. Genuine busy exhaustion and WALL_REPLAYS_MAX are unchanged.

Delivery is at-least-once: a crash between the wake and settlement replays once
more (marked, bounded). Tests: predecessor->successor exactly-once, storage
failure, schedule-while-retired, exact-profile wake, durable success/stop fences.
